[Chapter "Without c4"]
[Line "Against the Jobava (2.Nc3 and Bf4)"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{Knight before the c-pawn, then Bf4. Exchange on d4 and take b5 away from the knight.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. Nc3 {The Jobava London: knight before the c-pawn.} 2... Nf6 {Develop.} 3. Bf4 c5 {Hit d4 at once.} 4. e3 cxd4 {Exchange in the centre.} 5. exd4 a6 {Take b5 away from the knight, so White's Nb5 ideas are gone.} 6. Nf3 Nc6 {Develop with pressure on d4.} 7. Ne5 Bd7 {Develop, so that if the knight takes on c6, Black recaptures with the bishop and keeps a healthy structure.} *
